    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d717">

                <pb facs="0750" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg492"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857Ib3/1</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Cork</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Frost</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Queenstown</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 31,
                            1915, noon.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Ship surgeon Burns, of <hi rendition="#italic">Iberian</hi>, American citizen,
                    states submarine did not shell <hi rendition="#italic">Iberian</hi> until latter
                    disregarded signal. Gave time to take boats. Wiley died shock, superficial
                    wounds. Cable me disposition remains. No other Americans injured.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
